{
  "version": "1.0",
  "license": "CC0-1.0 (hand-written, not copied from any printed dictionary)",
  "about": [
    "Structured companion to dictionary.json. An entry is a JSON object so new",
    "words can carry a type, a dialect region, an example, a source and a",
    "confidence instead of living in a flat one-word-one-string map.",
    "",
    "Fields:",
    "  id         optional stable id, defaults to the iraqi text",
    "  iraqi      the Iraqi surface form (may contain spaces = a phrase)",
    "  fusha      the MSA rendering",
    "  type       word | phrase | clitic | pronoun | particle | function",
    "  region     one or more of baghdad / south / mosul / west / general",
    "  tags       free-form labels used by the coverage report",
    "  example    a short Iraqi sentence showing the entry in context",
    "  source     where the rendering comes from (manual, reviewed, corpus)",
    "  confidence 0..1, how sure we are of the rendering",
    "  override   true when the entry deliberately replaces a dictionary.json",
    "            value (documented, so validate.py can list every override)",
    "  note       why the entry exists",
    "",
    "Spelling rule: no entry and no example carries tashkeel.  normalize()",
    "removes it before matching and a mark is not a word boundary, so the data",
    "is written «خدام» and «كنور».  A shadda in dictionary.json is different —",
    "there it separates two words (سدة «a dam» vs سدّه «he sealed it») and is",
    "therefore kept."
  ],
